repository-code: https://github.com/RatkoNikolic/srb-legal-rag
license: Apache-2.0
date-released: "2026-08-10"
keywords:
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - legal NLP
  - benchmark
  - knowledge graph
  - temporal validity
  - Serbian
abstract: >-
  A Serbian legal question-answering system and an exploratory benchmark built on
  it: the same legal question answered by five instrumented retrieval
  architectures — context stuffing, naive RAG, advanced hybrid retrieval, a typed
  temporal knowledge graph, and a bounded agentic loop — over one shared knowledge
  base, with accuracy, provenance fidelity, temporal correctness, latency and cost
  measured side by side. Every retrievable unit carries its law, article, version
  and validity interval, so a citation can be checked and a repealed provision can
  be told apart from one in force. Includes a negative result: on this corpus
  typed graph structure is statistically indistinguishable from strong flat
  retrieval. Saša Mirković (https://github.com/SasaMirkovic) co-designed the
  ingestion pipeline and the knowledge base, and advised on the retrieval
  architecture and on the evaluation design. The benchmark question sets
  under goldens/ are licensed CC BY 4.0 and are cited separately from the code.
